# FrontDesk Architecture

## Widget Shell
- `src/widgets/frontdesk/frontdesk-widget.tsx` drives the sidebar navigation and provider tab layout.
- Sidebar list entries route to `/frontdesk/{section}`; keep `list` definitions, route handling, and tab slugs synchronized.
- `PrimaryTabsComponent` renders provider views; ensure `providerSlugs` reflects the tab order and any new providers.
- `SideBarContainer` expects a pure `side` renderer—avoid embedding stateful logic inside the sidebar.

## Provider Blueprint
```
providers/{provider}/
├── {provider}-provider-view.tsx   # Entry point rendered inside PrimaryTabsComponent
├── components/
│   ├── conversation/              # toolbar, header, thread, reply box
│   ├── sidebar/                   # folder + filter UI
│   └── shared/                    # provider primitives (loading, empty states)
├── hooks/                         # data orchestration, mutations, UI state
└── types/                         # provider-scoped interfaces
```
- Reuse `BaseProviderView` so each provider keeps the same three-column layout.
- Pass dedicated `conversationListComponent` and `authModalComponent` props rather than reimplementing the frame.
- Provider hooks should expose a consistent contract: connection state, collections, selection handlers, composer control, and pagination/search helpers.

## Routing & Shared State
- Use router params `{ frontdeskRoute, provider }` as the source of truth for selected sidebar item and tab.
- Shared messaging data belongs in `src/store/messaging.ts`; reset atoms when switching channels or disconnecting providers.
- Keep provider-specific atoms/selectors co-located under the provider folder to avoid unintended coupling.

## Async & Data Flow
- REST calls live under `src/services/api-service/frontdesk/`; update placeholder URLs once backend endpoints firm up.
- Provide `refresh`, `loadMore`, `selectConversation`, and `handleSendReply` behaviors from hooks so base views stay declarative.
- Use optimistic updates with temporary IDs that line up with internal messaging types to keep confirmation flows predictable.

## Naming & Hygiene
- Components: `PascalCase.tsx`; hooks: `useName.ts`; util files: `{name}.utils.ts`.
- Promote reusable UI into `src/widgets/frontdesk/components/shared/` to minimize duplication.
- Co-locate tests (`*.test.tsx`) next to the components they cover when adding coverage.
